    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0660" n="646" sameAs="frus:frus1949v05/pg646"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Kirk, Alan G.: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-13T18:00:00+03:00">August 13, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2039. Embtel 1975, August 8.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d374-f1"/> Appointment made for
                    Monday, 15th, 10 p. m. Am informing British, French colleagues.</p>
                <p>Upon conclusion, visit intend reply anticipated queries American press
                    representatives substantially as follow: interview at my request to pay courtesy
                    visit on Generalissimo Stalin with only general conversation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d374-f1" n="1" xml:id="d374-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. Ambassador Kirk informed the Department that he had made the request
                    for an appointment with Stalin during a visit with Vyshinsky. (123 Kirk, Alan
                    G.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
